# op:// references only, into vault `watcher` — never values. Resolved by run.sh.
# Items are referenced by id where the title has a space (a rename would otherwise break every run).
CONTROLLER_HOST=op://watcher/awx-watcher/hostname
CONTROLLER_OAUTH_TOKEN=op://watcher/awx-watcher/token
# GRAFANA_TOKEN / GRAFANA_URL were here until 2026-10-17. No check reads Grafana any more — metrics
# and logs are ours — and two of them still REQUIRED these, so an expired Grafana token would have
# stopped the sweep with a message naming a system it no longer used. The `Grafana Watcher` item in
# vault `watcher` is now unreferenced and the owner can delete it (the agent cannot write that vault).
# Item "aiven-watcher" — a READ-ONLY Aiven application-user token on project `aware`. Never the
# agent-ops token: DreamHost administers this box as root.
AIVEN_TOKEN=op://watcher/aiven-watcher/token
# Gmail canary (objective gmail-healthy). The URL is not a secret, so it is pinned here. The token is
# item "n8n-gmail-canary": a Header Auth token that can trigger the canary and nothing else.
GMAIL_CANARY_URL=https://n8n.prod.rods.me/webhook/gmail-canary
GMAIL_CANARY_TOKEN=op://watcher/n8n-gmail-canary/token
# METRICS come from our own VictoriaMetrics (switched 2026-10-07) and LOGS from our own VictoriaLogs
# behind the same vmauth (2026-10-09, after 24 runs in which every log query matched Loki). One READ
# token for both: vmauth routes it to the query APIs only. The URL and the pinned certificate are not
# secrets.
#
# METRICS_BACKEND / LOGS_BACKEND were set here and are gone (2026-10-17): the switches themselves were
# removed. Their defaults were `grafana` and `loki`, so anything that did NOT set them queried an empty
# stack and believed the answer — which is how `estate-status.py`, run by hand, reported "NOTHING FROM
# SOUTH IS REPORTING" about a healthy estate for nine days. One backend cannot be selected wrongly.
VM_QUERY_URL=https://vps71884.dreamhostps.com:8427
VM_CA_FILE=/home/rods_pinky/watcher/victoriametrics-ca.crt
VM_READ_TOKEN=op://watcher/vm-reader/token
